VTID-04279 — commands run to build and verify this change

1. User-approved backlog security investigation surfaced two findings from
   route-auth-scanner-v1's missing_auth finding (efec84e4): approvals.ts
   and governance-controls.ts had zero real auth. User explicitly
   approved: "fix approvals.ts and governance-controls.ts now (add real
   auth, same pattern as their working siblings) in one careful,
   well-tested PR".

2. `grep -rn "router\.use(requireAdminAuth" services/gateway/src/routes/*.ts`
   -> confirmed the established sibling pattern: admin-navigator.ts:55,
   feedback-admin.ts:33, specialists-admin.ts:46.

3. Read requireAdminAuth (auth-supabase-jwt.ts:643-697) — requireAuth
   (Bearer JWT signature verify) + requireExafyAdmin
   (app_metadata.exafy_admin===true, 403 otherwise).

4. Read approvals.ts and governance-controls.ts in full. Confirmed:
   - approvals.ts: no auth import at all, on any of 6 routes; write routes
     call the internal autonomous-pr-merge endpoint with automerge:true.
   - governance-controls.ts: getUserInfo() read x-user-id/x-user-role
     straight off req.headers, zero signature verification;
     canModifyControls() checked that unverified role string against an
     allowlist. Confirmed app.js:9427 sends exactly this spoofable header
     from a plain client-side JS variable.

5. Before editing, audited EVERY internal same-process caller of both
   routes (not just the routes themselves), per the "careful" instruction:
   - grep "adminHeaders(id)" -> governance-tools.ts, admin-governance-
     tools.ts: sent { 'x-user-id': id.user_id, 'x-user-role': 'admin' } —
     the exact spoofable shape the route used to trust.
   - grep "approvalsApi(" -> developer-tools.ts: sent NO headers at all.
   - Compared against the established, correct pattern already used by
     admin-feedback-tools.ts/admin-users-rbac-tools.ts/observability-
     tools.ts/etc: authHeaders(id) = id.user_jwt ?
     {Authorization:`Bearer ${id.user_jwt}`} : {}.
   - grep "/api/v1/approvals|/api/v1/governance/controls" across
     services/gateway/src -> found a THIRD internal caller not part of the
     ORB voice tool layer: services/gemini-operator.ts's Operator Console
     "Developer Assistant" approval tools (executeDevListApprovals/
     executeDevApprovalCount/executeDevApproveItem/executeDevRejectItem)
     — calling routes/approvals.ts over HTTP with
     `Authorization: Bearer ${SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE}` (a real Supabase DB
     credential, not a user JWT).
   - Read verifyAndExtractIdentity()/extractIdentity() (auth-supabase-
     jwt.ts) to confirm precisely what would happen: the service-role JWT
     is signed with the same SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET, so requireAuth's
     signature check PASSES, but extractIdentity() reads
     app_metadata.exafy_admin from the payload — absent on a service-role
     token, so exafy_admin resolves false and requireExafyAdmin 403s it.
     Confirmed this caller would silently break once requireAdminAuth was
     added, unless fixed in the same PR.
   - Checked whether gemini-operator.ts's tool dispatcher has access to
     the real caller's raw JWT at the point these 4 functions run: no —
     only `args`/`threadId` are threaded through (confirmed by reading the
     ~3985 case-statement call sites); the VTID-03851 getThreadAuth(
     threadId) store only keeps {user_id, exafy_admin: boolean}, not the
     raw token, by design.

